[section, $md:
    # Builder packages

    The selected project builder supplies packages tied to its artefact model.
    This keeps browser and rendering APIs out of the core language.

    Every registered Builder package name sits below the reserved `@builder`
    root, at an explicit path the builder chooses. The exact root is not
    importable, and project-local packages cannot claim it. The HTML builder's
    static source package publishes through a directly contained
    `@package.moth`, and its binding-backed packages carry no source facade.

    The HTML builder provides static URLs through `@builder/web/site`,
    binding-backed runtime drawing through `@builder/web/canvas`, WebGL2
    rendering through `@builder/web/graphics` and live browser state through
    `@builder/web/page`. The universal `@core/html` and `@core/css` Core
    packages are available under every builder and documented in
    @../core/ (Core packages). The
    @../../progress/packages-and-builders (packages and builders progress matrix)
    records current support and accepted next gaps.

    ## Package pages

    - @./canvas/ (@builder/web/canvas)
    - @./graphics/ (@builder/web/graphics)
    - @./site/ (@builder/web/site)
    - @./page/ (@builder/web/page)
]

